From: fabt <46858378+fabiantorrestech@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 19:05:14 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] fix(grayscale): never switch off a filter Curbox did not
 switch on

Curbox now tracks whether it owns the system grayscale filter and leaves
filters from the user or other apps (e.g. GrayScaler+) alone:

- Ownership is claimed only after the filter is seen on following
  Curbox's own enable; a timed-out enable claims nothing.
- If the filter goes off while Curbox owns it, someone else took over and
  Curbox gives up ownership.
- Commands are serialized so an async Shizuku "off" cannot overtake an
  earlier "on".
- Ownership is persisted in noBackupFilesDir so a restore cannot bring
  back a stale value.

GrayScaleFilter only routes its enable/disable calls through
GrayscaleOwner, keeping the patch small on top of upstream.

